          "filename": "Middle school students lend a hand for Russell Lake Clean-up Campaign (10019352526).jpg",
          "caption": "ELBERTON, Ga. – Students from Elbert County Middle School's Future Farmers of America (FFA) donated their time to pick up trash at the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Richard B. Russell Lake, Sept. 18, 2013. Their effort was part of the Russell Project's annual clean-up campaign in honor of National Public Lands Day. The students collected about 60 pounds of garbage around the lake. Last year, students from Elberton Middle FFA built blue bird boxes that were placed around the lake.",
          "alt": "ELBERTON, Ga. – Students from Elbert County Middle School's Future Farmers of America (FFA) donated their time to pick up trash at the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers Richard B. Russell Lake, Sept. 18, 2013. Their effort was part of the Russell Project's annual clean-up campaign in honor of National Public Lands Day. The students collected about 60 pounds of garbage around the lake. Last year, students from Elberton Middle FFA built blue bird boxes that were placed around the lake.",
